      "side": 1,
      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] **Functionality (Endianness Bug)**: The previous `fourcc_to_string` implementation used bitwise shifts `(value \u003e\u003e (index * 8)) \u0026 0xFF`, which safely extracted `a` first regardless of the target\u0027s endianness. Replacing this with `std::bit_cast\u003cstd::array\u003cuint8_t, sizeof(value)\u003e\u003e` relies on memory layout, which means on big-endian targets, `bytes[0]` will be `d` instead of `a`.\n\nPlease restore the bitwise shift logic to ensure correct behavior across all platforms:\n```cpp\n\texplicit constexpr FpFourCc(uint32_t value) noexcept : chars_{}\n\t{\n\t\tfor (size_t i \u003d 0; i \u003c sizeof(value); ++i) {\n\t\t\tconst uint8_t ch \u003d (value \u003e\u003e (i * 8)) \u0026 0xFF;\n\t\t\tchars_[i] \u003d (ch \u003e\u003d 0x20 \u0026\u0026 ch \u003c\u003d 0x7e) ? static_cast\u003cchar\u003e(ch) : \u0027.\u0027;\n\t\t}\n\t}\n```\n[🔗](http://go/tj/42e0b4a9-ede8-4d05-b16c-437dbd626b32)",
